nL224:         * 【95†Test Strips, Papers & Readers】\nL225:         * 【111†Turbidimetric Analysis】\nL226:       * 【112†Reference Materials】\nL227:         * 【113†Amino Acid, Peptide & Protein Standards】\nL228:         * 【114†Biomarker & Metabolite Standards】\nL229:         * 【115†Cannabis Standards】\nL230:         * 【116†Carbohydrate Standards】\nL231:         * 【117†Certified Reference Materials】\nL232:         * 【75†Chromatography Standards】\nL233:         * 【118†Food Additive Standards】\nL234:         * 【119†Food & Cosmetic Component Standards】\nL235:         * 【120†ICP & AAS Standards】\nL236:         * 【121†Inorganic Elemental Impurity Mix Standards】\nL237:         * 【122†Ion Chromatography Standards】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nC:\\Program Files\\WERCS50\\DOCS\\wercs.ps (https://www.spectrumchemical.com/media/sds/P2630_MSDS.pdf)\nciteturn15view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 10; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.spectrumchemical.com/media/sds/P2630_MSDS.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 440\nL0@P0: MATERIAL SAFETY DATA SHEET\nL1@P0: 1. CHEMICAL PRODUCT AND COMPANY IDENTIFICATION\nL2@P0: Product code: P2630\nL3@P0: Product Name: DL-PANTOTHENIC ACID CALCIUM SALT\nL4@P0: Chemical Name: No information available\nL5@P0: Synonyms: Calcium DL-Pantothenate\nL6@P0: (+-)-N-(2,4-Dihydroxy-3,3-dimethylbutyryl)-beta-alanine\nL7@P0: DL-Pantothenic acid hemicalcium Salt\nL8@P0: Recommended use: No information available.\nL9@P0: CAS #: 63409-48-3\nL10@P0: Formula: C18-H32-Ca-N2-O10 or C9-H16-N-O5.1/2Ca\nL11@P0: RTECS # Not available\nL12@P0: CI#: Not available\nL13@P0: Supplier: Spectrum Chemicals and Laboratory Products, Inc.\nL14@P0: 14422 South San Pedro St.\nL15@P0: Gardena, CA 90248\nL16@P0: (310) 516-8000\nL17@P0: Emergency Telephone Number: CHEMTREC: 1-800-424-9300\nL18@P0: Contact Person: Martin LaBenz (West Coast)\nL19@P0: Contact Person: Chris Terpak (East Coast)\nL20@P0: 2. HAZARDS IDENTIFICATION\nL21@P0: OSHA Regulatory Status This material is not considered hazardous by the OSHA Hazard Communication\nL22@P0: Standard (29 1910.1200)\nL23@P0: EMERGENCY OVERVIEW\nL24@P0: May cause skin and eye irritation. May cause irritation of respiratory tract.\nL25@P0: Product code: P2630 Product name: DL-PANTOTHENIC\nL26@P0: ACID CALCIUM SALT\nL27@P0:  1 / 10\nL28@P0: Personal Protective Equipment\nL29@P0: Odor:\nL30@P0: No information available\nL31@P0: Physical state:\nL32@P0: Solid.\nL33@P0: Appearance:\nL34@P0: Powder.\nL35@P0: NFPA\nL36@P0: Color:\nL37@P0: White. Off-white.\nL38@P0: See Section 8.\nL39@P0-1: HMIS2. HAZARDS IDENTIFICATION\nL40@P1: Chronic Potential Health Effects:\nL41@P1: Component Carcinogen Status:\nL42@P1: DL-Pantothenic Acid Calcium Salt\nL43@P1: 63409-48-3 (100)\nL44@P1: No information available\nL45@P1: Target Organs: No information available\nL46@P1: Teratogenic Effects: No information available\nL47@P1: Mutagenic Effects: No information available\nL48@P1: Aggravated Medical Conditions: No information available\nL49@P1: See Section 11 for additional Toxicological Information\nL50@P1: POTENTIAL ENVIRONMENTAL EFFECTS\nL51@P1: No information available\nL52@P1: 3. COMPOSITION/INFORMATION ON INGREDIENTS\nL53@P1: Components CAS-No. Weight %\nL54@P1: DL-Pantothenic Acid Calcium Salt 63409-48-3 100\nL55@P1: 4. FIRST AID MEASURES\nL56@P1: General Advice: Poison information centres in each State capital city can provide additional\nL57@P1: assistance for scheduled poisons (13 1126)\nL58@P1: Skin Contact: Wash off immediately with soap and plenty of water removing all contaminated\nL59@P1: clothes and shoes. Get medical attention if irritation develops.\nL60@P1: Eye Contact: Flush eye with water for 15 minutes. Get medical attention if irritation occurs. If\nL61@P1: symptoms persist, call a physician.\nL62@P1: Eye Contact:\nL63@P1: May cause eye irritation.\nL64@P1: Acute Potential Health Effects:\nL65@P1: Inhalation:\nL66@P1: May cause irritation of respiratory tract.\nL67@P1: Principal Routes of Exposure:\nL68@P1: Ingestion. Inhalation.\nL69@P1: Ingestion:\nL70@P1: No information available. Expected to be a low hazard.\nL71@P1: Product code: P2630 Product name: DL-PANTOTHENIC\nL72@P1: ACID CALCIUM SALT\nL73@P1: Skin Contact:\nL74@P1: May cause skin irritation.\nL75@P1:  2 / 10\nL76@P1-2: POTENTIAL HEALTH EFFECTSInhalation: Move to fresh air. If breathing is difficult, give oxygen. In case of shortness of breath,\nL77@P2: give oxygen. Get medical attention.\nL78@P2: Ingestion: Do not induce vomiting without medical advice. Never give anything by mouth to an\nL79@P2: unconscious person. Consult a physician if necessary.\nL80@P2: Notes to Physician: Treat symptomatically\nL81@P2: 5. FIRE-FIGHTING MEASURES\nL82@P2: Flammable Properties\nL83@P2: Flashpoint (°C/°F): No information available.\nL84@P2: Tested according to:\nL85@P2: Not available\nL86@P2: Lower Explosion Limit (%): No information available\nL87@P2: Upper Explosion Limit (%): No information available\nL88@P2: Autoignition Temperature (°C/°F): Not applicable.\nL89@P2: Suitable Extinguishing Media: Carbon dioxide (CO2). Dry chemical. Water spray mist or\nL90@P2: foam.\nL91@P2: Unsuitable Extinguishing Media: No information available.\nL92@P2: Hazardous Combustion Products: Carbon monoxide; Carbon dioxide\nL93@P2: Specific hazards: May be combustible at high temperatures.\nL94@P2: Special Protective Equipment for Firefighters: As in any fire, wear self-contained breathing apparatus\nL95@P2: pressure-demand, MSHA/NIOSH (approved or equivalent)\nL96@P2: and full protective gear\nL97@P2: Specific Methods: No information available.\nL98@P2: 6. ACCIDENTAL RELEASE MEASURES\nL99@P2: Personal Precautions:\nL100@P2: Ensure adequate ventilation. Use personal protective equipment. Avoid contact with skin, eyes and clothing. Avoid dust\nL101@P2: formation. Remove all sources of ignition.\nL102@P2: Environmental Precautions:\nL103@P2: No information available.\nL104@P2: Methods for Cleaning Up:\nL105@P2: Sweep up and shovel into suitable containers for disposal. Avoid dust formation. Clean contaminated surface thoroughly.\nL106@P2: 7. HANDLING AND STORAGE\nL107@P2: Handling\nL108@P2: Product code: P2630 Product name: DL-PANTOTHENIC 3 / 10\nL109@P2-3: ACID CALCIUM SALTTechnical Measures/Precautions:\nL110@P3: Provide sufficient air exchange and/or exhaust in work rooms. Avoid dust formation. All equipment used when\nL111@P3: handling the product must be grounded. Keep away from incompatible materials.\nL112@P3: Safe Handling Advice:\nL113@P3: Wear personal protective equipment. Avoid contact with skin, eyes and clothing. Avoid dust formation. Do not\nL114@P3: ingest. Do not breathe vapours/dust. Keep away from heat and sources of ignition. Handle in accordance with good\nL115@P3: industrial hygiene and safety practice.\nL116@P3: Storage\nL117@P3: Technical Measures/Storage Conditions:\nL118@P3: Keep containers tightly closed in a dry, cool and well-ventilated place. Keep refrigerated. Keep at temperatures\nL119@P3: between 2 and 8 °C. Store away from incompatible materials.\nL120@P3: Incompatible Products:\nL121@P3: Oxidizing agents.\nL122@P3: 8. EXPOSURE CONTROLS / PERSONAL PROTECTION\nL123@P3: Engineering measures to reduce exposure: Ensure adequate ventilation. Use process enclosures, local\nL124@P3: exhaust ventilation, or other engineering controls to keep\nL125@P3: airborne levels below recommended exposure limits. If user\nL126@P3: operations generate dust, fume or mist, use ventilation to\nL127@P3: keep exposure to airborne contaminants below the exposure\nL128@P3: limit.\nL129@P3: Personal Protective Equipment\nL130@P3: Eye protection: Safety glasses. Safety glasses with side-shields.\nL131@P3: Skin and body protection: Long sleeved clothing. Chemical resistant apron. Gloves.\nL132@P3: Respiratory protection: Wear respirator with dust filter..\nL133@P3: Hygiene measures: Avoid contact with skin, eyes and clothing. Wash hands before breaks and\nL134@P3: immediately after handling the product. When using, do not eat, drink or smoke.\nL135@P3: National occupational exposure limits\nL136@P3: United States\nL137@P3: U.S Occupational Exposure Limits: Not determined\nL138@P3: Components OSHA NIOSH ACGIH AIHA WHEEL\nL139@P3: DL-Pantothenic Acid Calcium Salt -\nL140@P3: 63409-48-3\nL141@P3: None None None None\nL142@P3: Canada\nL143@P3: Canada Occupational Exposure Limits: Not determined\nL144@P3: Components Alberta British Columbia Ontario Quebec\nL145@P3: DL-Pantothenic Acid Calcium Salt\nL146@P3: 63409-48-3\nL147@P3: None None None None\nL148@P3: Australia and Mexico\nL149@P3: Occupational Exposure Limits for Australia and Mexico: Not determined\nL150@P3: Components Australia Mexico\nL151@P3: DL-Pantothenic Acid Calcium Salt\nL152@P3: 63409-48-3\nL153@P3: None None\nL154@P3: Product code: P2630 Product name: DL-PANTOTHENIC 4 / 10\nL155@P3-4: ACID CALCIUM SALT9. PHYSICAL AND CHEMICAL PROPERTIES\nL156@P4: 10. STABILITY AND REACTIVITY\nL157@P4: Stability: Stable at normal conditions\nL158@P4: Conditions to avoid: Heat. Avoid dust formation. Dust may form explosive mixture in air. Fine dust\nL159@P4: dispersed in air in sufficient concentrations, and in the presence of an ignition source\nL160@P4: is a potential dust explosion hazard. Incompatible materials.\nL161@P4: Materials to avoid: Strong oxidising agents.\nL162@P4: Hazardous decomposition\nL163@P4: products:\nL164@P4: Carbon monoxide. Carbon dioxide.\nL165@P4: Possibility of Hazardous\nL166@P4: Reactions:\nL167@P4: No information available\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn15view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/sds/sigald/262072\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://www.sigmaaldrich.com/sds/sigald/262072: (404) Not Found-------------------------------------------------