nL83: * * *\nL84: \nL85: Properties\nL86: \nL87: ### Quality Segment\nL88: \nL89: 【7†200】\nL90: \nL91: ### agency\nL92: \nL93: JP, USP, according to EP\nL94: ### sterility\nL95: \nL96: non-sterile\nL97: \nL98: ### form\nL99: \nL100: granular\nL101: \nL102: ### composition\nL103: \nL104: Dextrose, 2%\nL105: \nL106: ### packaging\nL107: \nL108: pkg of 500 g\nL109: \nL110: ### manufacturer/tradename\nL111: \nL112: GranuCult^{®} prime\nL113: \nL114: ### storage condition\nL115: \nL116: dry media (Keep tightly closed)\nL117: \nL118: ### technique(s)\nL119: \nL120: microbiological culture: suitable\nL121: \nL122: ### color\nL123: \nL124: light yellow\nL125: \nL126: ### pH\nL127: \nL128: 5.5-5.7 (22 °C, 30 g/L in H_{2}O, after autoclaving)\nL129: \nL130: ### solubility\nL131: \nL132: 30 g/L\nL133: \nL134: ### bulk density\nL135: \nL136: 640 kg/m^{3}\nL137: \nL138: ### application(s)\nL139: \nL140: clinical\nL141: microbiology\nL142: \nL143: ### storage temp.\nL144: \nL145: 15-25°C\nL146: ### suitability\nL147: \nL148: molds, yeasts\nL149: \nL150: Description\nL151: \nL152: ### General description\nL153: \nL154: GranuCult^{®} prime SABOURAUD-2% dextrose broth (According to harm. EP/USP/JP) is used for the cultivation and isolation of yeasts and molds as well as the absence test for Candida albicans. The high concentration of dextrose, in addition to the low pH, promotes the growth, the formation of spores (Conidia and Sporangia), and the formation of pigments of yeasts and molds. It also inhibits the growth of bacteria.\nL155: ### Application\nL156: \nL157: GranuCult^{®} prime SABOURAUD-2% dextrose broth is suitable for the cultivation of dermatophytes, yeasts, and molds. It can also be used for sterility testing and the determination of the fungi-static activity of pharmaceutical and cosmetical products.\nL158: ### Features and Benefits\nL159:   * GranuCult^{®} offers superior granulated culture media\nL160:   * Safe and sustainable due to reduced risks associated with fine dust and toxic substance inhalation, resulting in a safer work environment\nL161:   * Excellent wettability, solubility, and free-flowing properties\nL162:   * Convenient, with minimal component separation and clumping, even under warm or humid conditions\nL163:   * High batch-to-batch reproducibility\nL164:   * Prolonged shelf life of up to five years\nL165:   * High number of test strains exceeding all regulatory demands\nL166:   * Granulation technology allows many supplements to be included, with no need to add these separately\nL167: ### Analysis Note\nL168: Appearance (clearness): clear\nL169: Appearance (colour): yellowish-brown\nL170: pH-value (25 °C): 5.4 - 5.8\nL171: Typical composition (g/litre): Peptone from meat 5.0; Peptone from casein 5.0; D(+)Glucose 20.0.\nL172: Growth (Trichophyton mentagrophytes ATCC 18748): good to very good\nL173: Growth (Trichophyton rubrum ATCC 28188): fair to good\nL174: Growth (Microsporum gallinae ATCC 12108): fair to good\nL175: Growth (Trichophyton ajelloi ATCC 28454): fair to good\nL176: Growth (Aspergillus brasiliensis (formerly A. niger) ATCC 16404 (WDCM 00053)): good to very good\nL177: Growth (Penicillium commune ATCC 10428): good to very good\nL178: Incubation: 7 days; 28°C\nL179: Growth promotion test in accordance with the harmonised method of EP, USP and JP.\nL180: Inoculum on reference medium (Candida albicans ATCC 10231 (WDCM 00054)): ≤ 100\nL181: Growth (Candida albicans ATCC 10231 (WDCM 00054)): fair to very good\nL182: Incubation: up to 3 days; 30-35°C\nL183: The information above is current at this time of publication and is subject to change without notice (except for customers holding a change control agreement with our company). The information/format can be altered at any time and inany way if internal company matters or Standard Regulationsdo say so.\nL184: ### Other Notes\nL185: \nL186:   * The appearance of the broth is clear and yellowish-brown.\nL187:   * The pH value at 25 °C is in the range of 5.4-5.8.\nL188: \nL189: ### Legal Information\nL190: \nL191: GRANUCULT is a registered trademark of Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany\nL192: \nL193: NutriSelect is a registered trademark of Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany\nL194: ### Disclaimer\nL195: \nL196: We offer two media types: the superior granulated GranuCult^{®} and the cost-efficient powdered^{®} culture media, depending on your needs. The designations basic, plus, or prime are added to indicate the quality control level, from basic quality control to standard QC plus to prime for full regulatory compliance.\nL197: \nL198: * * *\nL199: \nL200: * * *\nL201: \nL202: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL203: \nL204: Explore all of our products under 【8†Sabouraud Dextrose broth】\nL205: \nL206: 【8†View All Products】\nL207: \nL208: * * *\nL209: \nL210: ## Safety Information\nL211: ### Storage Class\nL212: \nL213: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL214: \nL215: * * *\nL216: \nL217: ## Documentation\nL218: \nL219: Certificate of Analysis[Button: Certificate of Quality]\nL220: \nL221: * * *\nL222: \nL223: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL224: \nL225: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL226: \nL227: Lot/Batch Number\nL228: \nL229: * * *\nL230: \nL231: Don't see the Right Version?\nL232: \nL233: If you require a particular version, you can look up a specific certificate by the Lot or Batch number.\nL234: \nL235: 【9†Search for a COA】\nL236: ### Already Own This Product?\nL237: \nL238: Find documentation for the products that you have recently purchased in the Document Library.\nL239: \nL240: 【10†Visit the Document Library】\nL241: \nL242: * * *\nL243: \nL244: * * *\nL245: \nL246: Related Categories\nL247: \nL248: 【11†Industrial Microbiology】\nL249: \nL250: 【12†Microbial Culture Media】\nL251: \nL252: * * *\nL253: \nL254: * * *\nL255: \nL256: Top\n"
